{"id": "EUVD-2026-80426", "enisaUuid": "803eaad5-9de0-3a06-bc16-539f771b777e", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/panthor: harden firmware build-info bounds checks\n\npanthor_fw_read_build_info() checks whether the metadata range fits in the\nfirmware image with hdr.meta_start + hdr.meta_size. Both fields are u32, so\nthe addition can wrap and let an out-of-bounds range pass validation.\n\nThe function also reads the \"git_sha: \" prefix without first checking that\nthe metadata is long enough, and meta_size == 0 can underflow the NULL\nterminator index.\n\nUse subtraction-based bounds checking and reject metadata that is too short\nto contain the expected prefix and trailing NULL byte.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T10:30:58", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:53:20", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5516f1acfd07564361cf306cc90a8e513df0f096", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6ae19dce3e8c13ae73590b3f4311abe9f96bbae8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8321b093fa6c297b80586460ce6914d9655df170"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-89826", "GHSA-vfmm-vgxh-2c77"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "04bdb769-84f0-3a98-ad36-2755d14cb6a9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "0c5969cf-cab8-37ac-9c29-6728b22a6cf9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2718d91816eeed03c09c8abe872e45f59078768c <8321b093fa6c297b80586460ce6914d9655df170"}, {"id": "30688c5e-7070-3348-9009-93f162a83e62", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.51"}, {"id": "462f5149-ac2a-38fb-9b97-c751c696c892", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2718d91816eeed03c09c8abe872e45f59078768c <6ae19dce3e8c13ae73590b3f4311abe9f96bbae8"}, {"id": "be8ef029-f5b6-30eb-bd5b-56db8e2ede94", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "c3458cb9-0e5e-37fc-90d3-bf3f7fcbe225", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.10"}, {"id": "cf1d00eb-c26c-3b1e-99c6-1dd838333f80", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.5"}, {"id": "f2ec4e21-a463-3052-8ed6-012ae55f2b46", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2718d91816eeed03c09c8abe872e45f59078768c <5516f1acfd07564361cf306cc90a8e513df0f096"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "af7edc7a-c186-3c77-a74c-b9da2b1c8620", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}